    "/v1/ledger/verify": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Verify this tenant's ledger chains \u2014 read-only, whole-tenant by default.\n\nThe audit ledger is the platform's memory of every call event, so the\ncheap question an operator asks is \"does it still verify?\" \u2014 not\n\"verify this one SID\". With no ``call_sid`` the whole tenant ledger is\nwalked, one chain per call, and the answer names every chain that does\nnot link. An empty ledger verifies (zero entries, zero violations):\nnothing to reconstruct is not a failing check.",
        "operationId": "verify_ledger_v1_ledger_verify_get",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
